WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.261 --> 00:00:14.504
Jo anticipated, her sisters were in awe of the Laurences' impressive estate.

2
00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:21.768
Even Mother paused to admire the elegant designs on the rugs as well as contemplate the splendid display

3
00:00:21.808 --> 00:00:23.029
of antiques in each room.

4
00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:27.451
"We are grateful for your hospitality," Mother thanked Mr.

5
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:35.102
Laurence. The Marches were served an eight-course meal, of which they now enjoyed the final portion: a decadent

6
00:00:35.162 --> 00:00:37.803
chocolate cake with tea exported from India.

7
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:44.905
Meg and Amy ate petite bites of the light, fluffy dessert, making sure not to show their teeth

8
00:00:45.085 --> 00:00:47.545
when they pulled the silver fork away from their mouth.

9
00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:54.327
With straight lady-like posture, they delicately patted the corners of their mouths after each nibble.

10
00:00:56.032 --> 00:01:00.554
Beth, who usually did not favor desserts, seemed to savor this particular one.

11
00:01:01.674 --> 00:01:08.417
Jo, unlike her more refined sisters, could not resist groaning in delight after each bite, causing Laurie to

12
00:01:08.477 --> 00:01:10.838
roll his eyes and make monkey faces at her.

13
00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:16.081
She returned the gesture, resulting in blasts of laughter from both parties.

14
00:01:17.061 --> 00:01:19.702
Shaking his head at Laurie but smiling, Mr.

15
00:01:19.742 --> 00:01:23.264
Laurence replied to Mother, "I am the one who is grateful.

16
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.163
Friendship with your daughters has changed my grandson immensely."

17
00:01:29.864 --> 00:01:33.246
To Mother, Laurie had become the son she never had.

18
00:01:33.266 --> 00:01:36.308
"He is a sweet, dear boy.

19
00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:39.010
You must be proud of him," she said.

20
00:01:39.871 --> 00:01:43.233
Perhaps it was Mother's sincerity and kindness that moved Mr.

21
00:01:43.253 --> 00:01:47.456
Laurence to speak openly about his most devastating losses in life.

22
00:01:47.476 --> 00:01:53.420
"Theodore, or Laurie, as he likes to be called, reminds me of his father.

23
00:01:54.292 --> 00:02:01.398
They both have the same mischievous attitude, the same rebellious streak, and the same talent for the arts.

24
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:09.145
I also had a little girl—the mildest, most adorable daughter parents could hope for.

25
00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:12.568
Your Beth reminds me of her so.

26
00:02:13.749 --> 00:02:20.394
My darling girl had a love for music, especially the piano, and she would play for my wife

27
00:02:20.475 --> 00:02:21.856
and me every evening.

28
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:29.504
How I would look forward to returning home to the sounds of music coming from the conservatory.

29
00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:37.928
My son, after he became a young man, went against my wishes, and followed his heart to Italy

30
00:02:38.429 --> 00:02:41.250
where he fell in love with a beautiful young woman.

31
00:02:42.131 --> 00:02:43.712
She was also an artist.

32
00:02:44.632 --> 00:02:53.157
They traveled across Europe with their small child, Laurie, living like gypsies—no permanent home, no decent food or

33
00:02:53.217 --> 00:03:01.420
clothing. I was furious, of course, and refused to support them financially unless they returned here and lived

34
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.621
like normal folks.

35
00:03:03.842 --> 00:03:09.444
Tragically, they died in an accident, leaving Laurie an orphan entrusted to my care."

36
00:03:09.464 --> 00:03:12.485
"You've raised a wonderful boy, Mr.

37
00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.526
Laurence," said Mother comfortingly.

38
00:03:15.687 --> 00:03:21.750
Mr. Laurence smiled sadly and said, "Although I may not say it to him enough, I am proud

39
00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.711
of my grandson."

40
00:03:22.731 --> 00:03:25.632
"What happened to your sweet daughter?"

41
00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.473
Mother gently inquired.

42
00:03:28.754 --> 00:03:31.275
Mr. Laurence's face was masked in pain.

43
00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:36.418
"She developed an illness when she was young and died of it."

44
00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:42.722
Mother remained silent as she looked at her girls, grateful that they were all in good health.

45
00:03:42.742 --> 00:03:46.804
"Grandfather?" Laurie broke the awkward silence.

46
00:03:47.676 --> 00:03:51.199
"Jo tells me that one of her sisters here has magic fingers.

47
00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:58.405
Apparently they glide effortlessly across the piano, creating the most beautiful melodies to the ears.

48
00:03:59.026 --> 00:04:05.971
Ouch!" Jo had just given Laurie a good strong kick to let him know how she felt about

49
00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.673
his unauthorized comment.

50
00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:15.359
As for Beth, she flushed pink as she slid lower into her chair and avoided eye contact with

51
00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:17.244
everyone. Mr.

52
00:04:17.284 --> 00:04:25.531
Laurence, already detecting Beth's shyness and reluctance to be in the spotlight, discreetly remarked, "I'm sure each young

53
00:04:25.611 --> 00:04:27.832
lady has a special talent of her own.

54
00:04:28.913 --> 00:04:32.836
Whether she chooses to show off that ability is her choice entirely.

55
00:04:33.717 --> 00:04:37.840
Now, I suggest we all go to the conservatory to relax."

56
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.424
Everyone stood up and followed the master of the estate to his most beloved room.

57
00:04:44.992 --> 00:04:49.716
The conservatory room offered delights for everyone according to individual tastes.

58
00:04:50.777 --> 00:04:55.141
For Meg and Amy, a most exotic arrangement of flowers and plants greeted them.

59
00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:58.824
"What an exquisite piece of creation!"

60
00:04:59.305 --> 00:05:03.108
exclaimed Amy, bending down to smell a lavender flower.

61
00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:10.194
Meg and Amy strolled around the room, whispering, and nodding their heads in approval at the enchanting display.

62
00:05:11.215 --> 00:05:15.951
For Jo, a shelf full of books prompted her to squeal like a little girl.

63
00:05:15.971 --> 00:05:20.314
"Have you ever seen anything so glorious?"

64
00:05:21.695 --> 00:05:25.037
"What's so glorious about an old bookshelf with smelly books?"

65
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.659
Laurie asked humorously.

66
00:05:26.679 --> 00:05:30.562
"It's what is inside them that makes them special!"

67
00:05:30.902 --> 00:05:33.924
said Jo as she ran her hand across the books' spines.

68
00:05:35.145 --> 00:05:39.028
However, it was Beth who felt the greatest pleasure of all.

69
00:05:40.392 --> 00:05:46.315
In one corner of the conservatory stood a stately grand piano, its lid rolled back as if to

70
00:05:46.375 --> 00:05:48.836
invite someone to touch its polished keys.

71
00:05:50.296 --> 00:05:56.079
As much as Beth's heart yearned to sit on the plush velvet stool and feel the ivory keys,

72
00:05:56.759 --> 00:05:59.120
she was too timid to act upon her desire.

73
00:06:00.061 --> 00:06:06.424
Her eyes never leaving the magical instrument that called to her, Beth inched away to the opposite side

74
00:06:06.444 --> 00:06:06.904
of the room.

75
00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.423
"This is my favorite room of the house," Mr.

76
00:06:11.463 --> 00:06:13.925
Laurence began in an unusually loud voice.

77
00:06:13.945 --> 00:06:18.929
"Unfortunately, during the day, nobody is around to enjoy it.

78
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:23.413
Even the servants don't come in here unless I give them permission.

79
00:06:24.474 --> 00:06:29.037
Everything here, especially that piano, is longing for some company.

80
00:06:29.818 --> 00:06:33.661
Too bad no one can give it the proper attention it deserves."

81
00:06:34.622 --> 00:06:36.584
Mr. Laurence shook his head regrettably.

82
00:06:37.788 --> 00:06:42.970
Out of the corner of his eye, he caught sight of Beth moving out slowly from behind a

83
00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.150
large armchair.

84
00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:49.192
"Could I perhaps impose on the kindness of your family?"

85
00:06:49.432 --> 00:06:54.093
Mr. Laurence continued, pretending that he didn't notice Beth's obvious interest.

86
00:06:55.154 --> 00:06:55.994
"Of course, Mr.

87
00:06:56.034 --> 00:07:01.976
Laurence," replied Mother, already discerning what the wise old man was about to suggest.

88
00:07:03.516 --> 00:07:08.618
"Would one of you be so kind as to come here once a day to make sure everything

89
00:07:08.759 --> 00:07:09.399
is in order?

90
00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:15.061
And perhaps, play on the piano keys so they don't get stuck or dusty?"

91
00:07:15.982 --> 00:07:19.363
Mr. Laurence pleaded, his eyes lingering on Beth.

92
00:07:19.383 --> 00:07:23.145
"Would you allow one to play the piano?"

93
00:07:23.545 --> 00:07:24.846
Jo asked innocently.

94
00:07:24.866 --> 00:07:32.401
"You could do as you like," the old man replied with a wink, "because when the conservatory door

95
00:07:32.501 --> 00:07:34.862
is closed, no one can hear anything.

96
00:07:36.143 --> 00:07:39.204
No one will be around to watch or bother you in any way.

97
00:07:39.904 --> 00:07:41.585
You will be completely alone."

98
00:07:42.785 --> 00:07:45.607
"Well, I would love to help you, Mr.

99
00:07:45.667 --> 00:07:51.369
Laurence," Jo replied heroically, "but I am working during the day, as is Meg.

100
00:07:52.269 --> 00:07:53.770
And Amy attends school."

101
00:07:53.790 --> 00:08:01.526
"Maybe I could help, sir," Beth spoke so softly no one heard her at first.

102
00:08:02.327 --> 00:08:05.089
Then she repeated it in a slightly louder voice.

103
00:08:05.109 --> 00:08:08.431
"Oh, would you, Beth, dear?

104
00:08:08.951 --> 00:08:09.732
Are you sure?"

105
00:08:10.753 --> 00:08:16.016
Mr. Laurence intentionally walked over to the piano and tapped his fingers on the keys.

106
00:08:17.437 --> 00:08:20.259
"Look at the sly fox," Laurie muttered to Jo.

107
00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:27.484
Jo nudged Laurie in agreement but kept her focus on Beth, whose footsteps directed her to the piano,

108
00:08:28.016 --> 00:08:30.439
as if a strong magnetic force was pulling her.

109
00:08:32.321 --> 00:08:35.865
Her trembling fingers reached out and lightly tapped the piano.

110
00:08:36.866 --> 00:08:40.511
Then with more boldness, she brushed it much like stroking a cat.

111
00:08:40.531 --> 00:08:48.560
"It would be my pleasure, sir," Beth replied honestly, giving the old man a soft, grateful smile.
